      <li><a href="#master-2026-calendar">1. Master 2026 Global DST Transition Schedule</a></li>
      <li><a href="#visual-timeline">2. Visual Timeline: Northern vs. Southern Hemisphere Cycles</a></li>
      <li><a href="#regional-rules">3. Regional Transition Rules &amp; Mathematical Algorithms</a></li>
      <li><a href="#southern-hemisphere">4. Southern Hemisphere DST Cycle (Reversed Seasons)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#three-week-gap">5. The "Three-Week Gap" Between US and EU Clock Shifts</a></li>
      <li><a href="#clock-change-mechanics">6. How Clocks Transition: 2:00 AM Local vs. 01:00 UTC</a></li>
      <li><a href="#multi-year-forecast">7. Future Transition Rule Engine (2026–2030)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#system-admin-checklist">8. System Administrator &amp; DevOps Readiness Checklist</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq-section">9. Frequently Asked Questions (20 Detailed FAQs)</a></li>
      <li><a href="#recommendations">10. Interactive Tools &amp; Related Guides</a></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <section id="master-2026-calendar" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="Master 2026 Calendar">
    <h2>1. Master 2026 Global DST Transition Schedule</h2>
    <p>
      Planning international travel, financial market operations, or remote meetings requires precise knowledge of transition dates across regions. Below is the master schedule of Daylight Saving Time start and end dates for major economic regions in 2026:
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Region / Country</th>
            <th>DST Spring Start Date (2026)</th>
            <th>DST Autumn End Date (2026)</th>
            <th>Transition Local Time</th>
            <th>Offset Change</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>United States &amp; Canada</strong></td>
            <td>Sunday, March 8, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, November 1, 2026</td>
            <td>02:00 Local Time</td>
            <td><a href="/est-vs-edt/">EST (UTC-5) ↔ EDT (UTC-4)</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>United Kingdom</strong></td>
            <td>Sunday, March 29, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, October 25, 2026</td>
            <td>01:00 UTC (01:00 Local)</td>
            <td><a href="/gmt-to-bst/">GMT (UTC+0) ↔ BST (UTC+1)</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>European Union (CET Zone)</strong></td>
            <td>Sunday, March 29, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, October 25, 2026</td>
            <td>01:00 UTC (02:00 Local)</td>
            <td><a href="/cet-to-est/">CET (UTC+1) ↔ CEST (UTC+2)</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Australia (NSW, VIC, SA, TAS)</strong></td>
            <td>Sunday, October 4, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, April 5, 2026</td>
            <td>02:00 Local Time</td>
            <td><a href="/aest-to-est/">AEST (UTC+10) ↔ AEDT (UTC+11)</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>New Zealand</strong></td>
            <td>Sunday, September 27, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, April 5, 2026</td>
            <td>02:00 Local Time</td>
            <td>NZST (UTC+12) ↔ NZDT (UTC+13)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Chile (Mainland)</strong></td>
            <td>Saturday, September 5, 2026</td>
            <td>Saturday, April 4, 2026</td>
            <td>24:00 Local Time</td>
            <td>CLT (UTC-4) ↔ CLST (UTC-3)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Israel</strong></td>
            <td>Friday, March 27, 2026</td>
            <td>Sunday, October 25, 2026</td>
