            <td>October 31, 2027</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>2028</strong></td>
            <td>March 12, 2028</td>
            <td>November 5, 2028</td>
            <td>March 26, 2028</td>
            <td>October 29, 2028</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>2029</strong></td>
            <td>March 11, 2029</td>
            <td>November 4, 2029</td>
            <td>March 25, 2029</td>
            <td>October 28, 2029</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>2030</strong></td>
            <td>March 10, 2030</td>
            <td>November 3, 2030</td>
            <td>March 31, 2030</td>
            <td>October 27, 2030</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 8 -->
  <section id="system-admin-checklist" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="System Admin Checklist">
    <h2>8. System Administrator &amp; DevOps Readiness Checklist</h2>
    <p>
      To prevent service outages, cron execution failures, or log corruption during clock change weekends:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ensure server system clocks are synchronized via Network Time Protocol (NTP) to Coordinated Universal Time (<a href="/gmt-vs-utc/">UTC</a>).</li>
      <li>Verify OS timezone packages (e.g., <code>tzdata</code> on Linux) are updated to the latest IANA release.</li>
      <li>Review automated scheduled tasks (cron jobs) running between 1:00 AM and 3:00 AM local time. For technical formatting rules, see our <a href="/iso-8601-date-time-format/">ISO 8601 date-time guide</a> and <a href="/unix-time-explained/">Unix time guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 9: FAQ SECTION -->
  <section id="faq-section" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions">
    <h2>9. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      {meta.faqs.map((faq) => (
        <div class="faq-item" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text);">{faq.q}</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6;">{faq.a}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

